{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"echo '### NCT00012376 derivation'; jq '.records[] | select(.nct_id==\\\"NCT00012376\\\")' packets/2026-09-11-pnh-vertical/universe-derivation.json; echo '### NCT00012376 raw key fields'; for f in .artifacts/source-cas/ctgov-live-20260906/evidence/raw/sha256/1e/1e0a9bbe959e38c122c9894782ff56b4ae3dc566179d199108c0af64eb56ab98.bin .artifacts/source-cas/ctgov-live-20260906/evidence/raw/sha256/c3/c3bdbe61b97e175e0a312cb37be064d3a74c38ada1c02dfde33e4e61a46fbdf3.bin; do jq -c '.studies[]? | select(.protocolSection.identificationModule.nctId==\\\"NCT00012376\\\") | {title:.protocolSection.identificationModule.briefTitle,conditions:.protocolSection.conditionsModule,description:.protocolSection.descriptionModule,interventions:.protocolSection.armsInterventionsModule.interventions}' \\\"\"'$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"echo '### NCT00012376 derivation'; jq '.records[] | select(.nct_id==\\\"NCT00012376\\\")' packets/2026-09-11-pnh-vertical/universe-derivation.json; echo '### NCT00012376 raw key fields'; for f in .artifacts/source-cas/ctgov-live-20260906/evidence/raw/sha256/1e/1e0a9bbe959e38c122c9894782ff56b4ae3dc566179d199108c0af64eb56ab98.bin .artifacts/source-cas/ctgov-live-20260906/evidence/raw/sha256/c3/c3bdbe61b97e175e0a312cb37be064d3a74c38ada1c02dfde33e4e61a46fbdf3.bin; do jq -c '.studies[]? | select(.protocolSection.identificationModule.nctId==\\\"NCT00012376\\\") | {title:.protocolSection.identificationModule.briefTitle,conditions:.protocolSection.conditionsModule,description:.protocolSection.descriptionModule,interventions:.protocolSection.armsInterventionsModule.interventions}' \\\"\"'$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"### NCT00012376 derivation\n{\n  \"nct_id\": \"NCT00012376\",\n  \"brief_title\": \"Chemotherapy Plus Sargramostim in Treating Patients With Refractory Myeloid Cancer\",\n  \"phase\": [\n    \"PHASE1\"\n  ],\n  \"overall_status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n  \"study_type\": \"\",\n  \"enrollment\": 35,\n  \"start_year\": \"\",\n  \"lead_sponsor\": \"National Cancer Institute (NCI)\",\n  \"collaborators\": [],\n  \"interventions\": [\n    \"bryostatin 1\",\n    \"laboratory biomarker analysis\",\n    \"pharmacological study\",\n    \"sargramostim\"\n  ],\n  \"source_locator\": {\n    \"page_sha256\": \"c3bdbe61b97e175e0a312cb37be064d3a74c38ada1c02dfde33e4e61a46fbdf3\",\n    \"array_index\": 47,\n    \"nct_id\": \"NCT00012376\"\n  }\n}\n### NCT00012376 raw key fields\n{\"title\":\"Chemotherapy Plus Sargramostim in Treating Patients With Refractory Myeloid Cancer\",\"conditions\":{\"conditions\":[\"Accelerated Phase Chronic Myelogenous Leukemia\",\"Adult Acute Myeloid Leukemia With 11q23 (MLL) Abnormalities\",\"Adult Acute Myeloid Leukemia With Del(5q)\",\"Adult Acute Myeloid Leukemia With Inv(16)(p13;q22)\",\"Adult Acute Myeloid Leukemia With t(15;17)(q22;q12)\",\"Adult Acute Myeloid Leukemia With t(16;16)(p13;q22)\",\"Adult Acute Myeloid Leukemia With t(8;21)(q22;q22)\",\"Blastic Phase Chronic Myelogenous Leukemia\",\"Chronic Myelomonocytic Leukemia\",\"Chronic Phase Chronic Myelogenous Leukemia\",\"Paroxysmal Nocturnal Hemoglobinuria\",\"Previously Treated Myelodysplastic Syndromes\",\"Recurrent Adult Acute Myeloid Leukemia\",\"Refractory Anemia\",\"Refractory Anemia With Ringed Sideroblasts\",\"Relapsing Chronic Myelogenous Leukemia\",\"Thrombocytopenia\",\"Untreated Adult Acute Myeloid Leukemia\"]},\"description\":{\"briefSummary\":\"Drugs used in chemotherapy use different ways to stop cancer cells from dividing so they stop growing or die. Colony-stimulating factors such as sargramostim may increase the number of immune cells found in bone marrow or peripheral blood and may help a person's immune system recover from the side effects of chemotherapy. Phase I trial to study the effectiveness of bryostatin 1 combined with sargramostim in treating patients who have refractory myeloid cancer\",\"detailedDescription\":\"PRIMARY OBJECTIVES:\\n\\nI. To determine the maximally tolerated dose of continuous intravenous infusion bryostatin-1 when given in combination with GM-CSF.\\n\\nII. To describe and quantify the frequency of toxicity of the combination of continuous intravenous infusion bryostatin-1 and subcutaneously administered GM-CSF.\\n\\nSECONDARY OBJECTIVES:\\n\\nI. To describe the impact of the combination of bryostatin-1 and GM-CSF on the differentiation and cell cycle distribution of myeloid cells in vivo.\\n\\nII. To describe the impact of the combination of bryostatin-1 and GM-CSF on T lymphocyte populations.\\n\\nIII. To assess the pharmacokinetics of continuous infusion bryostatin-1.\\n\\nOUTLINE: This is a dose-escalation study of bryostatin 1.\\n\\nPatients receive bryostatin 1 IV continuously and sargramostim (GM-CSF) subcutaneously once daily on days 1-21. Treatment repeats every 28 days for 4 courses in the absence of disease progression or unacceptable toxicity. Patients with disease stabilization or improvement may continue treatment for up to 12 courses.\\n\\nCohorts of 2 patients receive escalating doses of bryostatin 1 until the maximum tolerated dose (MTD) is determined. The MTD is defined as the dose at which 30% of patients experience dose-limiting toxicity.\\n\\nPROJECTED ACCRUAL: A maximum of 45 patients will be accrued for this study within 12-18 months.\"},\"interventions\":[{\"type\":\"DRUG\",\"name\":\"bryostatin 1\",\"description\":\"Given IV\",\"armGroupLabels\":[\"Treatment (bryostatin 1 and sargramostim)\"],\"otherNames\":[\"B705008K112\",\"BRYO\",\"Bryostatin\"]},{\"type\":\"BIOLOGICAL\",\"name\":\"sargramostim\",\"description\":\"Given subcutaneously\",\"armGroupLabels\":[\"Treatment (bryostatin 1 and sargramostim)\"],\"otherNames\":[\"GM-CSF\",\"Leukine\",\"Prokine\"]},{\"type\":\"OTHER\",\"name\":\"laboratory biomarker analysis\",\"description\":\"Correlative studies\",\"armGroupLabels\":[\"Treatment (bryostatin 1 and sargramostim)\"]},{\"type\":\"OTHER\",\"name\":\"pharmacological study\",\"description\":\"Correlative studies\",\"armGroupLabels\":[\"Treatment (bryostatin 1 and sargramostim)\"],\"otherNames\":[\"pharmacological studies\"]}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
